 "equipment_type": "Pump (diesel fire pump controller)",
 "applies_to": "FFL700DP and FFL800DP diesel engine fire pump controllers (built-in RS-485, optical port, EXP1012T/EXP1013T modules on FFL800DP), per protocol document I557 GB I 11 17.",
 "summary": "The Lovato FFL700DP and FFL800DP are diesel engine fire pump controllers (EN 12845). They speak Modbus RTU, ASCII or TCP on the built-in RS-485, the optical port and, on FFL800DP, expansion modules. This map covers mains voltage, engine speed, hours, engine temperatures, oil pressure, fuel level, battery voltages, the alarm words, I/O states, the global status word and the reset/save commands.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU",
  "ASCII",
  "TCP"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baud": 9600,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": 1001
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "1-based",
  "note": "The tables print hex addresses one above the request address; the document says to subtract one, and its example reads battery A voltage (table 0F0Eh) by sending 0F 0D. Addresses here are already reduced by one."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "FFL700DP - FFL800DP diesel engine fire pump controllers - Communication protocol Modbus",
  "doc_number": "I557 GB I 11 17",
  "revision_date": "2017-11-08",
  "url": "https://datasheet.lovatoelectric.com/DOWNLOAD/Technical/TechInstructions/33.%20CONTROLLORI%20ANTINCENDIO/I557IGB11_17.pdf",
  "pages": "pp. 1-3 (settings, functions, example), pp. 7-10 (Tables 2-5)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Measures and status words are read with function 03 or 04 (same data) and are listed as input registers. Commands use function 06.",
  "Function 06 writes only to addresses above 1000h.",
  "Word order: the example answer 00 00 04 B7 decodes to 1207 = 12.07 VDC (battery A, VDC/100), so 32-bit values are high word first (ABCD). The example's own wording calls the register 'number of switching alarms of breaker 1', a leftover from another product; the address and value match battery A.",
  "Temperatures, oil pressure, fuel level and water reserve are printed with alternative units (°C / °F, bar / psi, % / l / gal); the protocol document does not say which one applies, so check the unit set on the controller (see its operating manual).",
  "Left out: the LIM1-8 limit words and CNT1-8 counters (user-defined), and the front-panel key simulation at 2F0Ah (its Italian and English key tables disagree).",
  "Ethernet (EXP1013T) defaults: IP 192.168.1.1, IP port 1001."
 ],
